.TH JAZZ 1 "2026-07-12" "jazz 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
jazz \- focus-video player for the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jazz
[\fB\-\-hd\fR|\fB\-\-ascii\fR] [\fIfile\fR|\fIurl\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
ffmpeg decodes a video into raw RGB frames (contrast-normalized so dark scenes
still have detail) and ffplay plays the audio invisibly in the background.
Frames render as real pixels via the Kitty graphics protocol by default.
.IP
With no
.IR file ,
jazz plays from
.IR ~/.config/jazz ,
using an fzf picker if several videos are present. Recognized extensions:
.IR .mp4 ", " .mkv ", " .mov ", " .webm ", " .m4v .
.IP
A
.I url
is handed to yt\-dlp, which resolves it to a direct stream that ffmpeg opens
like a file \(em seeking and looping still work. Needs yt\-dlp installed. The
resolved links are signed and expire after a few hours.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-hd
Render each cell as a 2x2 block of pixels using quadrant characters.
.TP
.B \-\-ascii
Render as painted ASCII text art instead of pixels.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit. Handled before the terminal is put into raw mode, so this
is the one invocation that works without a TTY.
.PP
There is no
.B \-\-json
and no other machine-readable mode:
.B jazz
is a player with no status or listing to serialise.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.BR ffmpeg ,
.BR ffprobe
and
.B ffplay
are required and checked up front, before the picker or the terminal is
touched. If any is missing jazz prints
.B jazz: needs <missing> on PATH (brew install ffmpeg)
and exits 1.
.BR yt\-dlp
is needed only for URLs and
.BR fzf
only when the library holds several videos.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B space
Pause / resume.
.TP
.B \(<-/\(->
Seek \(+-10s.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B JAZZ_LOG=\fIpath\fR
Write per-frame timing lines to
.IR path .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/jazz
Default video library.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Help was shown, the fzf picker was cancelled, or playback ended with
.BR q .
.TP
.B 1
ffmpeg, ffprobe or ffplay is not on PATH; there are no videos in
.IR ~/.config/jazz ;
several videos are present but fzf is missing; a URL was given but yt\-dlp is
missing or could not resolve it; the file does not exist
.RI ( "no such file" );
or ffprobe could not read it.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR ffplay (1),
.BR fzf (1),
.BR yt\-dlp (1)
